# Easy compilation of cspot using provided Dockerfile

The dockerfile mounts the root of the repository and compiles it. 
Output binaries are in `build/bin`

This does assume you have cloned and ran `git submodule update --init
--recursive` first.


## Steps:

> All steps assume that your working directory is the root of the repository.

Steps:
1. Create the compiler docker image.
`sudo docker build . -t cspot-compiler`

2. Run `./build.sh` to compile. This passes in the right arguments into `docker run`. 

3. Have fun cspoting :)